.TH CCZE 1 "August 2026" "ccze-rs 0.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccze \- colorize, analyze, and verify streaming logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccze
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccze
reads log records from standard input and writes them to standard output.
It recognizes syslog, web access, and JSON records without changing their
payload bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-raw-ansi
Always emit ANSI color sequences.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plugin " " NAME
Select auto, syslog, httpd, or json parsing.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-plugins
List available parsers and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-color auto|always|never
Control ANSI output. The default is auto.
.TP
.B \-\-analytics
Enable rolling line-length and error-frequency anomaly detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-analytics-window " COUNT"
Set the rolling analytics window size.
.TP
.BI \-\-anomaly-threshold " SCORE"
Set the anomaly z-score threshold.
.TP
.B \-\-verify-protocol
Validate Start, Authenticate, Bind, and Ready event ordering.
.TP
.B \-\-backend-info
Print compiled native backend information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-vector-encode
Write one versioned, fixed-width metric vector per input record. Requires
.BR \-o .
.TP
.B \-\-vector-decode
Render metric summaries from a vector file. Requires
.BR \-\-vector-input .
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Set the vector output file.
.TP
.BI \-\-vector-input " FILE"
Set the vector input file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
journalctl -f | ccze
.PP
tail -f /var/log/messages | ccze -A | less -R
.PP
ccze --analytics --verify-protocol < service.log
.PP
ccze --analytics --vector-encode -o service.cczev < service.log
.PP
ccze --vector-decode --vector-input service.cczev
